hen you're just  tired in this salad  we get this salad mix from whole foods  it's called sweet kale mix or something  like that  um and it's my favorite it's so good and  i'll do like a honey ginger vinaigrette  and i'll add some raisins and some  cashews to it i love a good quickie meal  like this you got your veg and your  fiber from the salad kit with some  cashews on top for healthy fats you got  your carbs from the microwavable rice  and some protein from the chicken and if  you just can't be bothered to like thaw  and cook your chicken you could even  pick up a rotisserie chicken and call it  a day this sounds awesome and i love  that despite all the carb hate all day  the girl ate some carbs so  we love a happy ending with food so  before i give you my summarizing  thoughts i want to address the title of  this video and whether or not what you  eat can directly result in a booty the  short answer is obviously  no growing the glute muscles aka the  booty requires eating enough to fuel  muscle growth which requires a stimulus  threshold to be met eating enough is  arguably more important than the  specifics of what but the training and  let's be honest genetics is also key as  for this week of eating it's a bit  challenging to get an accurate picture  of daisy's daily intake as this video  was less of a what item a day and more  like random meals that i had this week  both on and off camera but overall i  would say the meals that we did see were  generally more or less balanced and  calorically adequate compared to my  previous review as we did have you know  some breakfast lunch dinner and some  snacks in between i was also pleasantly  surprised that despite all the carb  shaming she actually served a decent  amount of carbs in her meals which will  better support her energy needs and  recovery so i think we're definitely on  the right track on that front what i do  think is a problem is the moralizing  language around carbs and the hesitancy  to eat them if 